# The compute sidecars every e2e compose file attaches. Same shape as
# versions.env in the databricks platforms, so a bump there can be copied here
# line for line.
#
# THE TWO RELEASES DIFFER ON PURPOSE. The agent stays on v0.32.0: from v0.33.0
# (fabric-emulator #352) it gives every agent session its own Spark Connect
# session with an EMPTY catalog, and this emulator sends each warehouse
# statement as its own session (`"sql-"+st.ID`, internal/server/sql.go), so a
# CREATE TABLE is gone by the next statement. e2e-delta, e2e-dbt and
# e2e-dbt-task all fail on the v0.36.0 agent; Sail 0.7.1 alone passes. Move the
# agent only together with a change to how sessions are chosen here.
#
#   _VERSION  the tag: the dependency the image carries (pysail, pyspark-client)
#   _DIGEST   the identity: which build exactly -- the tag is rebuilt and
#             overwritten by every fabric-emulator release
#   _RELEASE  the fabric-emulator release that published that digest
#
# The compose files cannot read this file, so each repeats these values as its
# `${VAR:-default}`. scripts/check_sidecar_pins.py fails when any of them
# disagrees with this file, and with --registry also when _RELEASE did not
# publish _DIGEST. To bump: edit here, copy the defaults into every
# e2e/*/docker-compose.yml, run `make pins`.
SAIL_ENGINE_VERSION=0.7.1
SAIL_ENGINE_DIGEST=sha256:0b37f65f41da5d9493f3e5a5479a622b14ba6ca51492b5a0ab886ed1ffcbb430
SAIL_ENGINE_RELEASE=0.36.0
SPARK_CLIENT_VERSION=4.2.0
SPARK_CLIENT_DIGEST=sha256:8983695ef6516fd1a7965335b830a3b69b98c773dfbc1fd3c8122faa76cdd348
SPARK_CLIENT_RELEASE=0.32.0
